(Bug #77: the append slot's primary was a hand-rolled copy of the general
 one and had never learned `nothing`, an element or byte read, or any
 possessive. Every form below compiled the moment it was wrapped in
 braces, which is what proved the refusal was the slot's and not the
 language's.)

a list called ys is [9, 8].
a map called m is {"k": 7}.
a buffer called b is "A".
a list called xs is [].

append nothing to xs.
append element 1 of ys to xs.
append byte 1 of b to xs.
append ys's first to xs.
append ys's last to xs.
append ys's length to xs.
append m's "k" to xs.

(The braced spellings, still reading the same.)
append {element 1 of ys} to xs.
append {m's "k"} to xs.

Print element 1 of xs.
Print element 2 of xs.
Print element 3 of xs.
Print element 4 of xs.
Print element 5 of xs.
Print element 6 of xs.
Print element 7 of xs.
Print element 8 of xs.
Print element 9 of xs.
Exit 0.
